  <prompt>
    Support **person-to-person direct threads** that are NOT anchored to a record, with **explicit exactly-two-participant membership**. This is R1's second thread topology alongside record-anchored (open) threads — ad-hoc named N-party group threads are explicitly deferred to a later phase.

    • A user can start a 1:1 thread with another user.
    • Membership is EXACTLY the two participants — no more, no less. Unlike open threads, membership does NOT derive from `MembershipResolverService` (there is no record anchor); it is the explicit two-party list.
    • The thread appears in EACH participant's authorized threads (both, and only, the two participants can read it).

    Build over the shared `IThreadResolver` (task 040) + thread model (task 004) + membership reconcile (task 041). A 1:1 thread has no ADR-024 regarding anchor — the thread topology field distinguishes it; task 041's reconcile projects its explicit two-party set to ACS membership; task 042's read filter honors the two-party visibility.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `Services/Communication/`, the thread model (task 004), `IThreadResolver` (task 040), membership derivation/reconcile (task 041), ADR-034, §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. You keep 1:1 as a thin topology over the existing thread machinery, not a parallel path.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A 1:1 direct thread topology exists: a user starts a 1:1 thread with another user; membership is exactly the two participants (explicit list, NOT ADR-034-derived — there is no record anchor); the thread appears in each participant's authorized threads and no one else's. It reuses the shared `IThreadResolver` + thread model + membership reconcile + access filter. Build clean; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported; Step 9.5 FULL gates run; `/conflict-check` clean before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec Owner Clarifications: R1 supports two thread topologies — record-anchored (matter/project via ADR-024 regarding) AND 1:1 direct (person-to-person, explicit two-party membership). Ad-hoc named group threads (N participants, not record-anchored) are deferred (design §1 out-of-scope, spec Assumptions).

      **Component Justification (§11) for the 1:1 topology:**
      1. **Existing** — The thread model (task 004), `IThreadResolver` (040), membership reconcile (041), and access filter (042) already exist. This task adds a topology discriminator + explicit-two-party membership path, not a new thread engine (verify by grep).
      2. **Extension** — Extend the thread model with a topology marker and give `IThreadResolver` / the membership-derivation path a branch: record-anchored → ADR-034; 1:1 → explicit two-party list. No new entity, no new pipeline.
      3. **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete failure)** — Without a 1:1 topology, a user cannot message another user directly (every thread would need a record anchor); FR-09 fails. And absent an EXPLICIT two-party membership branch, a 1:1 thread has no membership source (ADR-034 needs a record), so it would either be inaccessible or wrongly derive members — a concrete FR-09/NFR-06 failure, not "future flexibility."

      **Scope discipline:** exactly-two-participant only. Do NOT build N-party group threads (deferred). Do NOT anchor 1:1 threads to a record (they are person-to-person). Reuse 041's reconcile (projecting the two-party set to ACS) and 042's filter (two-party visibility) — do not fork them.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IThreadResolver.cs (task 040 — find-or-create, add 1:1 branch)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (task 004 — `sprk_communicationthread` topology/participant fields)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ThreadMembershipDerivationService.cs (task 041 — explicit two-party branch)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs (task 042 — two-party visibility)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ (endpoint to start a 1:1 thread)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-09">Support person-to-person direct threads NOT anchored to a record, with explicit two-participant membership. A user can start a 1:1 thread; membership is exactly the two participants; it appears in each participant's authorized threads.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Exactly-two-participant only. Ad-hoc named N-party group threads are DEFERRED — MUST NOT build them in R1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Open (record-anchored) membership derives from `MembershipResolverService`; 1:1 does NOT — it uses the explicit two-party list. Do not force a record anchor onto a 1:1 thread.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Record-anchored threads use the regarding family; a 1:1 thread has no regarding anchor — distinguish via the thread topology field, MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse task 041's reconcile (project the two-party set to ACS membership) and task 042's access filter (two-party visibility) — do not fork them. ACS membership for a 1:1 = exactly the two participants.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register any new service/endpoint via `CommunicationModule`; DI unconditional (ADR-032 if feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

