  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read task 040's `IThreadResolver`, task 004's thread topology/participant fields, task 041's derivation service, and task 042's access filter to find the extension points for a 1:1 topology.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + root §11 + ADR-034 (open vs explicit membership) before adding the topology.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a thread topology discriminator (record-anchored vs 1:1-direct) to the thread model usage; a 1:1 thread carries no ADR-024 regarding anchor and stores the explicit two-participant set.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend `IThreadResolver` with a 1:1 branch: find-or-create a person-to-person thread keyed by the ordered participant pair (so starting a 1:1 with the same person twice reuses the thread, not creates a duplicate).</step>
    <step order="5">Extend the membership-derivation path (task 041) so a 1:1 thread returns the EXPLICIT two-party list (not ADR-034-derived); confirm task 041's reconcile projects exactly those two to ACS membership.</step>
    <step order="6">Add a BFF endpoint to start a 1:1 thread with another user (authZ; both participants get ACS identities via task 010's identity map); confirm task 042's access filter makes the thread visible to exactly the two participants.</step>
    <step order="7">Register any new service/endpoint via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional.</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests (closed set incl. negative cases): a user starts a 1:1 thread with another user; membership is EXACTLY the two participants; it appears in EACH participant's authorized threads; a THIRD user does NOT see it (negative/authorization case); starting a 1:1 with the same person reuses the thread (no duplicate); a 1:1 thread has no regarding anchor.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` then `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-043-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: exactly-two membership, third-user exclusion, no N-party leakage, reuse of 041/042, §11 justification); `adr-check` against `spec.md`. Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="9.6">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (043 ✅) + reset `current-task.md`; record decisions (topology discriminator, ordered-pair keying, explicit-membership branch).</step>
  </steps>

